{{also|Azure|azuré}}
==English==
{{wp}}
[[File:Azure Heraldic Shield.svg|right|thumb|The arms of Berington of Chester are <!--per Harleian manuscript no. 1535--> simply ''azure''.]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|asure}}, from {{der|en|fro|azur}}, derived from {{der|en|ar|لَازَوَرْد|t=lapis lazuli}}, dropping the '''''l''''' as if it were equivalent to the French article {{m|fr|l'}}. The Arabic is from {{der|en|fa-cls|لاجورد|tr=lājward|t=lapis lazuli}}, from the region of Lajward in [[Badakhshan]].

Compare with {{cog|it|azzurro}} and {{cog|es|azul}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈæʒə/|/ˈæz.jʊə/|/ˈæʒjʊə/|/əˈzjʊə/|a=UK}}, {{q|rarely}} {{IPAchar|/ˈeɪ.ʒə/}}<!-- ever /ˈæʒɔː/, /əˈʒʊə/ ? -->
** {{audio|en|En-uk-azure.ogg|a=RP}}
** {{homophone|en|Asia|qq1={{IPAchar|/ˈeɪʒə/}}}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈæʒɚ/|/ˈæz.jʊɹ/|a=US}}<!-- ~/-jɚ/-->, {{IPAchar|/əˈzʊɹ/}}, {{IPAchar|/əˈʒʊɹ/}}<!-- ~/-ˈʒɝ/-->, {{q|rarely}} {{IPAchar|/əˈzjʊɹ/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-azure.ogg|a=US}}
<!-- check: * {{IPA|en|/æzˈjʉːə/|/əˈʒʉə/|a=Australia}} -->
* {{rhymes|en|ʊə(ɹ)|ɜː(ɹ)|s=2}}
: {{IPAchar|/ˈæʒə(ɹ)/}} is the first (sometimes only) pronunciation listed in many dictionaries<ref name="MWO">{{R:MWO}}</ref><ref name="OED">{{R:New English Dictionary}} ([https://www.oed.com/dictionary/azure_n?tab=pronunciation modern OED online], [https://archive.org/details/in.ernet.dli.2015.99992/page/n641/mode/2up?view=theater 1933 print edition])</ref><ref name="DC">{{R:Dictionary.com}}</ref><ref name="OLeD">{{R:Oxford Learner's Dictionaries}}</ref><ref name="Cambridge">{{R:Cambridge}}</ref><ref name="Longman">[https://www.ldoceonline.com/dictionary/azure Longman Dictionary of Contemporary English, "azure"]</ref> and is the most commonly used.<ref name="TR">See data in [[Wiktionary:Tea room/2022/February#azure_pronunciation_issue|the February 2022 Tea Room]].</ref> Second-most commonly mentioned is {{IPAchar|/ˈæzjʊə(ɹ)/}}.<ref name="OED"/><ref name="OLeD"/><ref name="Cambridge"/><ref name="Longman"/> Though missed by most other dictionaries<!-- besides Wiktionary-->, {{IPAchar|/əˈz(j)ʊə(ɹ)/}} and {{IPAchar|/əˈʒʊə(ɹ)/}} with stress on the second syllable are also common<!-- , constituting perhaps 20-35% of modern uses-->.<ref name="TR"/>
* Other, uncommon<ref name="TR"/> pronunciations are {{IPAchar|/ˈæʒʊə(ɹ)/}}<ref name="Collins">{{R:Collins}}</ref> and {{IPAchar|/ˈæʒjʊə(ɹ)/}}<ref name="OED"/><ref name="Longman"/> In older English, {{IPAchar|/ˈeɪ-/}}<!-- /ˈeɪʒə/~/ˈeɪʒj(ʊ)ə/~/ˈeɪzjʊə/ --> also occurred and is still recorded in some dictionaries,<ref name="OED"/> but rarely used.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable|and|uncountable}} The clear blue colour of the sky; also, a pigment or dye of this colour.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1815|author=w:William Wordsworth|title=s:Extracts from An Evening Walk
|passage=In robes of '''azure'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2014|author=w:William H. Gass|title=On Being Blue: A Philosophical Inquiry| page=59| passage=For our blues we have the '''azures''' and ceruleans, lapis lazulis, the light and dusty, the powder blues, the deeps: royal, sapphire, navy, and marine {{...}}}}
#: {{color panel|azure|007FFF}}
# {{lb|en|tincture}} A [[blue]] colour on a [[coat of arms]], represented in engraving by horizontal parallel lines.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1904|author=Arthur Charles Fox-Davies|title=The Art of Heraldry: An Encyclopaedia of Armory|publisher=London : T.C.; & E.C. Jack|page=41
|text=Berington of Chester (on the authority of Harleian manuscript No. 1535) is said to bear a plain shield of azure. Personally I doubt this coat of arms {{nb...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1997|author=Brault|title=Early Blazon|passage=In ''Bb'' [Glover's Roll], the conventional letter ''B'' is used to indicate '''azure''' in most items.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=E. Baumgaertner Wm E. Baumgaertner|author2=Wm E. Baumgaertner|title=Squires, Knights, Barons, Kings: War and Politics in Fifteenth Century England|publisher=Trafford Publishing|isbn=9781426907692
|text=Sir Henry "Hotspur" Percy: before 1399: or, a lion rampant '''azure''', differentiated with a label gules (a blue lion rampant on a field of gold, differentiated with a red label signifying the first-born son) {{...}} }}
#: {{color panel|azure (heraldry)|0028E9}}
# {{lb|en|poetic}} The unclouded sky; the blue vault above.
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=I|passage=Not like those steps / On heaven's '''azure'''.|year=1873}}
#* {{RQ:Blind Ascent of Man|poem=Reapers|page=140|passage=Not a single cloud mars the flawless '''azure'''; / Not a shadow moves o'er the moveless crops; [...]}}
# Any of various widely distributed [[lycaenid]] butterflies of the [[genus]] {{taxfmt|Celastrina|genus}}.
# Any of various Australasian [[lycaenid]] butterflies of the genus {{taxlink|Ogyris|genus}}.
# [[lapis lazuli|Lapis lazuli]].

