===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=adjective|:inh|enm:awake<ety:from<awaken<ety:inh<ang:āwacan>>>>|tree=1}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*weǵ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|awake}}, a shortened form of {{m|enm|awaken|t=awakened, awake}}, past participle of {{der|en|enm|awaken|t=to awaken}}. See verb below. Compare {{cog|stq|woak|t=awake}}, {{cog|nds-de|waak|t=awake}}, {{cog|de|wach|t=awake}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|more}} {{tlb|en|[[predicative]] only}}

# {{lb|en|incomparable}} Not [[asleep]]; [[conscious]].
#: {{syn|en|conscious|lucid|wide awake|Thesaurus:awake}}
#: {{ant|en|asleep|unconscious|Thesaurus:asleep}}
#: {{ux|en|We've lain '''awake''' [[a good many]] nights worrying about her.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2000|author=w:Bill Oddie|title=Gripping Yarns|page=86|passage=By quarter to six all this had me so '''awake''' and agitated that even the Balinese wind chimes that I hung up in the garden to relax me began to sound like Big Ben.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative|by extension}} [[alert|Alert]], [[aware]].
#: {{syn|en|wary|woke|Thesaurus:vigilant}}
#: {{ant|en|heedless|oblivious}}
#: {{ux|en|They were '''awake''' to the possibility of a decline in sales.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1845|title=The Sportsman's Magazine of Life in London and the Country|page=355
|passage=The Baker was a [[two-handed]] hitter, and seemed perfectly '''awake''' to the business before him.}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Pickwick Papers|passage=‘Sammy,’ whispered Mr. Weller, looking cautiously round; ‘{{...}} Me and a cab’net-maker has dewised a plan for gettin’ him out. A pianner, Samivel—a pianner!’ {{...}}<br>‘And wot ‘ud be the good o’ that?’ said Sam.<br>‘Let him send to my friend, the cabinet-maker, to fetch it back, Sammy,’ replied Mr. Weller. ‘Are you '''avake''', now?’<br>‘No,’ rejoined Sam.<br>‘There ain’t no vurks in it,’ whispered his father. ‘It ‘ull hold him easy, vith his hat and shoes on, and breathe through the legs, vich his holler. {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1965|month=June|author=w:Martin Luther King, Jr.|title=Remaining Awake Through a Great Revolution|url=https://www2.oberlin.edu/external/EOG/BlackHistoryMonth/MLK/CommAddress.html
|passage=And so we see in our own world a revolution of rising expectations. The great challenge facing every individual graduating today is to remain '''awake''' through this social revolution.}}

