# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To go in the [[reverse]] [[direction]].
#: {{ux|en|The train '''backed''' into the station.}}
#: {{ux|en|The horse refuses to '''back'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=1|passage=Thinks I to myself, “Sol, you’re run off your course again. This is a rich man’s summer ‘cottage’ {{nb...}}.” So I started to '''back''' away again into the bushes. But I hadn’t '''backed''' more’n a couple of yards when I see something so amazing that I couldn’t help scooching down behind the bayberries and looking at it.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1954|month=January|author=H. P. White|title=Vignettes of the Rail|journal=Railway Magazine|page=54, at Harmon station, New York|text=No sooner had a waiting locomotive '''backed''' on to its train, the vociferous 4-6-4 or 4-8-4 re-emerged from under the bridge, and the two red marker lights on the last vehicles passed, than the headlight of the electric engine hauling the following train could be seen under the bridge and the waiting queue of locomotives had moved up one.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2026-07-16|work=Skip Boring|title=Inside the 2004 Brianna Maitland Case: One of Vermont’s Most Haunting Mysteries|author=Nicholas Muhoro|url=https://skipboring.com/brianna-maitland-disappearance-vermont/|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260721020617/https://skipboring.com/brianna-maitland-disappearance-vermont/|text=It was Brianna’s Oldsmobile, and it had been '''backed''' into the side of the abandoned house with enough force that the rear bumper was caught on the foundation. The back tyres were actually lifted off the ground.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[support]].
#: {{ux|en|I '''back''' you all the way.}}
#: {{ux|en|Which horse are you '''backing''' in this race?}}
#* {{RQ:Melville Moby-Dick|chapter=32|page=148|text=Be it known that, waiving all argument, I take the good old fashioned ground that the whale is a fish, and call upon holy [[w:Jonah|Jonah]] to '''back''' me.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1933|author=w:Frank Clune|title={{w|Try Anything Once (book)|Try Anything Once}}|location=Sydney|publisher=Angus and Robertson|page=153|passage=The pony won three times in one month and as I had '''backed''' it on each occasion I collected a ‘bank’ of over &pound;400.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=June 9, 2012|author=Owen Phillips|work=BBC Sport| title=[http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/18138777 Euro 2012: Netherlands 0-1 Denmark]| passage=And Netherlands, '''backed''' by a typically noisy and colourful travelling support, started the second period in blistering fashion and could have had four goals within 10 minutes}}
#* {{quote-web
|en
|date=September 15, 2022
|title=China lodges complaint as U.S. Senate panel advances Taiwan bill
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220915115333/https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/china-lodges-complaint-us-senate-panel-advances-taiwan-bill-2022-09-15/
|archivedate=15 September 2022
|work=w:Reuters
|section=Asia Pacific
|text=The Senate Foreign Relations Committee '''backed''' the Taiwan Policy Act of 2022 by 17-5, despite concerns about the bill in U.S. President Joe Biden's administration and anger about the measure from Beijing.}}
# {{lb|en|nautical|of the wind}} To [[change]] [[direction]] [[contrary]] to the [[normal]] [[pattern]]; that is, to shift [[anticlockwise]] in the northern hemisphere, or [[clockwise]] in the southern hemisphere.
# {{lb|en|nautical|of a square sail}} To [[brace]] the [[yard]]s so that the [[wind]] presses on the [[front]] of the sail, to [[slow]] the [[ship]].
# {{lb|en|nautical|of an anchor}} To lay out a second, smaller [[anchor]] to provide additional holding power.
# {{lb|en|UK|of a hunting dog}} To stand still behind another dog which has pointed.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To push or force backwards.
#: {{co|en|to '''back''' oxen}}
#: {{ux|en|The mugger '''backed''' her into a corner and demanded her wallet.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1887|author=Harriet W. Daly|title=Digging, Squatting, and Pioneering Life in the Northern Territory of South Australia|page=279|passage=The soil seems to be very good; the creek runs through the reserve, and has a dam thrown across it, which '''backs''' the water for a very considerable distance, and enables them to irrigate a portion of their cultivation block.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To get upon the back of; to [[mount]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 4-1|act=II|scene=iii|passage=I will '''back''' him [a horse] straight.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1902|author=John Buchan|title=The Outgoing of the Tide
|passage=The horse was the grey stallion he aye rode, the very beast he had ridden for many a wager with the wild lads of the Cross Keys. No man but himself durst '''back''' it, and it had lamed many a hostler lad and broke two necks in its day.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To place or seat upon the back.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Cymbeline|act=V|scene=v|passage=Great Jupiter, upon his eagle '''backed''', / Appeared to me.}}
# To make a back for; to furnish with a back.
#: {{co|en|to '''back''' books}}
# To adjoin behind; to be at the back of.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Measure|act=IV|scene=i|passage=He hath a garden circummured with brick,<br>Whose western side is with a vineyard '''backed'''}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1877|author=w:Thomas Henry Huxley|title=Physiography: An Introduction to the Study of Nature
|passage=the chalk cliffs which '''back''' the beach}}
#* {{RQ:Ferguson Zollenstein|IV
|passage=So this was my future home, I thought!{{...}}'''Backed''' by towering hills, the but faintly discernible purple line of the French boundary off to the southwest, a sky of palest Gobelin flecked with fat, fleecy little clouds, it in truth looked a dear little city; the city of one’s dreams.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1960|month=December|author=Voyageur|title=The Mountain Railways of the Bernese Oberland|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=752|text=So we continue climbing to the saddle of the Kleine Scheidegg, where ahead there comes into view the wide expanse of the Grindelwald valley, '''backed''' by the snowy crown of the Wetterhorn.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Search For John Lennon|author=Lesley-Ann Jones|year=2020|text=I Feel Fine — single, '''backed''' by "She's A Woman"}}
# To write upon the back of, possibly as an [[endorsement]].
#: {{co|en|to '''back''' a letter;&emsp; to '''back''' a note or legal document}}
# {{lb|en|legal|of a justice of the peace}} To sign or endorse (a warrant, issued in another county, to apprehend an offender).
# To [[row]] [[backward]] with (oars).
#: {{co|en|to '''back''' the oars}}
# {{cln|en|contranyms}}{{lb|en|MLE|transitive}} To [[draw]] from [[behind]] the back (a [[knife]] etc.) {{gloss|as also {{m|en|back out}}}}.
#* {{quote-song|en|date=2017-08-04|artist={{w|Zone 2 (rap group)|Zone 2}} (Kwengface x Trizzac x PS)|title=Sticks and Stones|url=https://genius.com/Zone-2-sticks-and-stones-lyrics|passage=Sticks and Stones may break my bones<br/>Not when I '''back''' this botty}}
#* {{quote-song|en|author=TwoLzz|title=TwentyTwo|date=2020-08-13|url=https://genius.com/Blacz-and-twolzz-twentytwo-lyrics|note=1:14–1:18|passage=When I '''back''' this blade, wallahi<br/>The hearts get beat like they just saw jihadi}}
