===Verb===
{{en-verb|+|+|+,book<l:dialectal>|+,~n<l:dialectal>}}

# To [[cook]] using an [[oven]], especially [[baked good]]s.
## {{lb|en|transitive|or|intransitive|or|ditransitive|with person as subject}} To cook (something) in an oven (for someone).
##: {{ux|en|I '''baked''' a delicious cherry pie.}}
##: {{ux|en|She's been '''baking''' all day to prepare for the dinner.}}
##: {{ux|en|He '''baked''' her a cake.}}
## {{lb|en|intransitive|with baked thing as subject}} To be cooked in an oven.
##: {{ux|en|The cake '''baked''' at 350°F.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|journal=w:San Francisco Chronicle|title=A salmon dish as a last hurrah for summer produce|date=September 18 2026|author=Octavio Peña|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260923232648/https://www.sfchronicle.com/food/recipes/article/roast-salmon-zucchini-tomato-22424434.php
|text=I use cherry tomatoes because they’re bite-size and '''bake''' quickly.}}
## {{lb|en|intransitive}} To regularly prepare baked goods.
##: {{ux|en|In some cultures, it is expected that a proper housewife should '''bake'''.}}
## {{lb|en|intransitive|slang|figurative}} To smoke [[marijuana]].
##: {{lb|en|Let's '''bake''' tonight.}}
## {{lb|en|figurative|with "in" or "into"}} To [[incorporate]] into something greater.
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=United States. Congress. Senate. Committee on Commerce, Science, and Transportation. Subcommittee on Aviation Operations, Safety, and Security|title=Airline Industry Consolidation: Hearing|page=36
|passage=Disagreements between pilots' unions are '''baked''' into the merger cake.}}
##* {{quote-text|en|year=2016|author=David B. Woolner; John M. Thompson|title=Progressivism in America: Past, Present and Future|page=100
|passage=Many of the causes of governmental dysfunction are simply '''baked''' into the cake of American politics and will never change.}}
# To heat or dry.
## {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be warmed for drying and hardening.
##: {{syn|en|[[fire]] (pottery in kilns)}}
##: {{ux|en|The clay '''baked''' in the sun.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To dry by heat.
##: {{ux|en|They '''baked''' the electrical parts lightly to remove moisture.}}
## {{lb|en|intransitive|figuratively}} To be [[hot]].
##: {{ux|en|It is '''baking''' in the greenhouse.}}
##: {{ux|en|I'm '''baking''' after that workout in the gym.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|figuratively}} To cause to be [[hot]].
##* {{quote-journal|en|year=2008|month=October|author=Davy Rothbart|title=How I caught up with dad|journal=w:Men's Health|volume=23|issue=8|issn=1054-4836|page={{gbooks|VMgDAAAAMBAJ|112|baked}}|passage=My dad told me about his days in the Navy: He'd agreed to be a guinea pig in exchange for a shorter enlistment. {{...}} They '''baked''' him in the sun.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|by extension|obsolete}} To harden by cold.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Tempest|I|ii|passage=The earth {{...}} is '''baked''' with frost.}}
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|book=V|canto=VII|stanza=9|passage=They '''bake''' their sides vppon the cold, hard stone.}}
# {{lb|en|computer graphics|transitive}} To [[fix]] ([[lighting]], [[reflection]]s, etc.) as part of the [[texture]] of an [[object]] to improve [[render]]ing [[performance]].

====Usage notes====
In the dialects of northern England, the simple past ''[[book]]'' and past participle ''[[baken]]'' are sometimes encountered.

The ''incorporate into something greater'' definition is often by an object that is a metaphorical cake, as in the example given: ''the causes of governmental dysfunction are simply '''baked''' into the cake of American politics''. It doesn't have to have such an object though, and the meaning doesn't change: ''the causes of governmental dysfunction are simply '''baked''' into American politics''.

