#* {{quote-book|en|year=1794|author=Erasmus Darwin|title=Zoonomia; Or, The Laws of Organic Life|page=36|text=These '''associate''' ideas are gradually formed into habits of acting together, by frequent repetition, while they are yet separately obedient to the will; as is evident from the difficulty we experience in gaining so exact an idea of the front of St. Paul's church, as to be able to delineate it with accuracy, or in recollecting a poem of a few pages.}}

